 "circuits": [],
 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Complement and marking",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The NPN complement is the MMBTA42. The top of the SOT-23 body carries the code 2D."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Package and assembly",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Moisture sensitivity is level 1 to J-STD-020, with a lead-free reflow peak of 260 °C. The mold compound has a UL 94V-0 flammability rating and is RoHS-compliant and halogen-free. The leads are solder plated and meet the solderability test of MIL-STD-750 Method 2026."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output characteristic",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "At 25 °C, base currents from -50 µA to -500 µA give collector currents of roughly 10 mA to 68 mA (in magnitude) once VCE is past a few volts, with a slow rise as VCE increases (Fig.1)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gain against current and temperature",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "At VCE = -10 V the gain is near 150 at 25 °C and near 200 at 100 °C, flat from -0.1 mA to some tens of milliamps, then drops off sharply above about -50 mA (Fig.2)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Saturation",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "With base current one tenth of collector current, VCE(sat) stays near -100 mV up to a few milliamps and climbs to about -200 mV (25 °C) or -280 mV (100 °C) at -50 mA. VBE(sat) runs from about -545 mV at -0.1 mA to about -810 mV at -100 mA at 25 °C, roughly 100 mV less in magnitude at 100 °C (Figs.3 and 4)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Base-emitter on voltage",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "At VCE = -10 V and 25 °C, VBE is about -600 mV at -1 mA of collector current; at 100 °C the same current needs about -490 mV (Fig.5)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Capacitance",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "At 1 MHz, input capacitance Cib falls from about 60 pF near zero bias to about 22 pF at -10 V; output capacitance Cob falls from about 18 pF to about 5 pF over the same range (Fig.6)."
  }
 ],
